1
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:06,020
Excuse me.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:07,460
Yes?

3
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:11,180
Where is Kameari Station?

4
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:16,300
Go straight down this road and turn left,
and you'll come out in front of the station.

5
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:18,480
I see. Thank you very much.

6
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:24,720
Excuse me, this may be a strange question,
but are you by any chance Mr. Tendo Yoshimi?

7
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:28,640
No, I'm not.
People often say I look like him, though.

8
00:00:36,940 --> 00:00:41,180
When you watch TV, keep the room bright
and sit back from the screen, all right?

9
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:54,300
Anyone who has no money, come to me.

10
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:59,100
I have none either, but don't worry.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,360
Look, the blue sky, the white clouds.

12
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:13,020
Somehow or other, it'll work out in time.

13
00:01:25,980 --> 00:01:29,980
Anyone who has no job, come to me.

14
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:34,560
I have none either, so don't worry.

15
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:41,640
Look, the burning steel too.

16
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:48,320
Somehow or other, it'll work out in time.

17
00:01:50,460 --> 00:01:53,580
You understand, right? Right, right.

18
00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:57,520
Once you understand,
keep quiet and follow me.

19
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:18,940
Now, we will begin.

20
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:34,020
C-Chief, this is finally happening!

21
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:36,140
Yes, it's finally happening.

22
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:50,760
W-why us?

23
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:55,460
The receiving station for the Kyoto Management Office's residence post has been decided:
the Ginza Police Box!

24
00:02:56,320 --> 00:02:58,480
Yes! Ohara-kun, the role!

25
00:02:58,680 --> 00:03:00,320
It's like a dream, Chief.

26
00:03:01,940 --> 00:03:03,900
Ohara-kun, c-chief...

27
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:06,220
Ohara-kun, Chief.

28
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:10,120
Senpai is being transferred?

29
00:03:10,480 --> 00:03:11,857
That's the way it is.

30
00:03:11,907 --> 00:03:15,299
After all, he's the nationwide number
one problem child among police officers.

31
00:03:15,349 --> 00:03:17,463
The number of reprimand
letters is astronomical,

32
00:03:17,513 --> 00:03:20,760
and Katsushika Police Box has always
been left in tears because of him.

33
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:27,250
Since it's grossly unfair to make Katsushika Police Box
alone shoulder the cleanup and responsibility for him,

34
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:29,400
this decision has been made.

35
00:03:29,900 --> 00:03:34,260
Still, the Ginza box chief agreed to take in his senior officer,
didn't he?

36
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:35,740
That takes real courage, doesn't it?

37
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:39,000
W-well, that's how should I put it...

38
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,720
Well, never mind the small details.

39
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:43,000
Anyway, this is cause for celebration.

40
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:47,460
Looking back, it's been so many
years since I became his superior.

41
00:03:50,220 --> 00:03:53,040
My blood pressure rose,
and my heart weakened.

42
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:57,340
Ever since, I've shouldered all of life's
seven calamities and eight sufferings.

43
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,540
Today I finally cut ties
with that wretched bond.

44
00:04:00,540 --> 00:04:03,060
For the police box,
the long winter has ended.

45
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:04,900
At last, spring is coming.

46
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:11,300
The chief is thrilled too, you know.

47
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:14,020
A special bonus to celebrate
getting rid of Ryotsu,

48
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:15,360
apparently being handed
out to every officer.

49
00:04:16,060 --> 00:04:17,960
Somehow, poor Ryo-chan.

50
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:22,300
Speak of the devil, here comes Ryotsu.

51
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:26,300
Ryo-chan, what's with that outfit?

52
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:29,160
Yeah, even Ryo got kicked out.

53
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:32,120
That's rough. Where are you going to live?

54
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:36,000
For the time being I'll be sleeping
at the police box at my new post.

55
00:04:36,637 --> 00:04:40,040
isn't that Mr. Ryotsu over there?

56
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:41,540
Mr. Ryotsu?

57
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:45,612
From today on,
you're no longer a clerk of ours,

58
00:04:45,662 --> 00:04:47,500
and you're not my subordinate either.

59
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:50,340
So naturally, the proper courtesy
is to address him with "-san."

60
00:04:50,340 --> 00:04:52,076
And Ryotsu-san,

61
00:04:52,126 --> 00:04:55,700
even if you just happen to be waiting nearby,
don't go speaking to me.

62
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:58,360
Happily,

63
00:04:58,360 --> 00:05:02,940
now we won't have to be yelled at all the time.
It's refreshing.

64
00:05:03,660 --> 00:05:06,820
What? I don't yell because I want to!

65
00:05:06,820 --> 00:05:09,060
It's all your fault.

66
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:10,640
See, there he goes yelling again.

67
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:12,380
Anyway, Chief, the thing is...

68
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:15,760
I'm no longer your superior, so...

69
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:17,160
You and I are strangers now.

70
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:19,180
Look, your ride's here.

71
00:05:20,060 --> 00:05:23,000
If anything happens, consult your new boss.

72
00:05:23,560 --> 00:05:24,780
Yes, goodbye.

73
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:26,020
Senpai

74
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:26,780
Ryo-chan

75
00:05:27,340 --> 00:05:28,520
Nakagawa! Reiko!

76
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,280
Take care of yourself!

77
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:32,400
No, Senpai! Take care!

78
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:34,800
Come visit us once in a while, Ryo-chan!

79
00:05:35,280 --> 00:05:38,705
Damn it! Once I'm gone from
the Kameari Kōen-mae Police Box,

80
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:42,900
this show will have to change its title!
Do you understand?!

81
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:45,960
He said that so casually, didn't he?

82
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:46,404
Senpai,

83
00:05:46,454 --> 00:05:50,080
did you only stop by
here to say that one line?

84
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:51,933
By the way, Ryo-chan,

85
00:05:51,983 --> 00:05:54,720
which Ginza police box
are you being assigned to?

86
00:05:54,720 --> 00:06:00,080
I think it's the Higashi-Ginza
Kabukiza-mae Police Box.

87
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:05,620
That's Ginza, it's definitely Ginza.

88
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:10,640
Everyone, come on over to our town!

89
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:15,380
Dear.

90
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:19,800
I went from the old downtown
straight to the middle of Tokyo.

91
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:24,380
Even the people walking
outside look different.

92
00:06:25,340 --> 00:06:29,120
And maybe because Kabukiza is next door,
there are old ladies everywhere, hey.

93
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:33,940
Hey, officer...

94
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:35,500
What?

95
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:39,540
Everyone from the Tachibana-kai
got separated from me somewhere.

96
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:41,040
Tachibana-kai?

97
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:44,140
You came for the Kabukiza revue, didn't you.

98
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:46,180
So everyone got separated, you say.

99
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,620
You're the one who got lost, aren't you?

100
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:50,500
Never mind which one it is.

101
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:52,400
Please help me find everyone.

102
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:53,560
Fine, fine.

103
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:02,700
Just because we're next
to the Kabuki-za Theatre,

104
00:07:03,140 --> 00:07:06,620
no matter which way I look,
all I see are old ladies who look the same.

105
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:10,860
Don't you remember what bus you came on?

106
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:14,400
I don't remember at all.

107
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:19,360
Tachibana-kai, Tachibana-kai,
Tachibana-kai...

108
00:07:19,840 --> 00:07:21,060
Oh my, oh my.

109
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:25,080
The old lady's gone!

110
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:28,600
Hey! Where did that old lady go?!

111
00:07:29,540 --> 00:07:32,840
Damn it! They all look the same!

112
00:07:33,060 --> 00:07:35,160
Hey! Where are you?!

113
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:37,730
There they are! Hey,

114
00:07:37,780 --> 00:07:39,940
Don't go getting lost again!

115
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:42,680
There are so many people,
my head's spinning!

116
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:45,420
This is quicker now!

117
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:50,880
Hey everyone,
does anyone know this old lady?

118
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,740
She's one of the Tachibana-kai ladies!

119
00:07:55,060 --> 00:07:57,900
There they are! It's Tate-san, over here!

120
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:02,480
Thank you so much, you really saved us.

121
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:06,120
No problem.
Just don't go getting lost again!

122
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:10,260
Oh no, I got swallowed up
by the wave of old ladies!

123
00:08:10,260 --> 00:08:10,720
Aaaaaah!

124
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:16,499
The power of these old ladies is incredible.

125
00:08:16,549 --> 00:08:18,640
No wonder they live so long.

126
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:19,920
Excuse me.

127
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:22,866
No sooner has one trouble
passed than another comes.

128
00:08:22,916 --> 00:08:24,700
A foreigner this time

129
00:08:25,300 --> 00:08:27,860
Would you tell me the word for
"department" to use?

130
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:31,037
No, no. I don't understand English at all.

131
00:08:31,087 --> 00:08:34,280
If you're coming to Japan,
learn to speak Japanese first.

132
00:08:34,540 --> 00:08:35,040
What's the matter?

133
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:37,373
What a pain. I'm fed up with this.

134
00:08:37,423 --> 00:08:40,400
This guy just keeps babbling nonsense,
blah, blah, blah.

135
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:40,900
Turn.

136
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:48,140
Me na he peru o I wars de
party mates turn yasukkain.

137
00:08:49,460 --> 00:08:51,680
Thank you.

138
00:08:55,980 --> 00:09:04,460
Wow, Yamashita, you're fluent in English! We study it every
day after duty ends. It's the team leader's policy here.

139
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:09,060
What? I've landed in a
completely crazy place.

140
00:09:09,060 --> 00:09:10,380
Ryotsu-kun.

141
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:13,300
Yes, Team Leader.

142
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:17,000
The traffic signal on Showa Street
at Ginza 7-chome has broken down.

143
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,640
Go direct traffic right away, please.

144
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:21,000
Ha

145
00:09:25,980 --> 00:09:28,640
I've never directed traffic before!

146
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:31,880
Like this, then like this... was it?

147
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:32,100
Hey,

148
00:09:33,540 --> 00:09:34,420
wait, that's wrong.

149
00:09:34,420 --> 00:09:35,940
Like this...

150
00:09:35,940 --> 00:09:36,560
Like this.

151
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:40,160
Idiot, what are you doing?

152
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:41,140
You're making a mess!

153
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:42,980
He's just talking like
he knows what he's doing.

154
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:48,060
At this rate, we're going to get killed.

155
00:09:48,060 --> 00:09:49,420
Hold on, hold on, just wait a second!

156
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:51,080
I'll go get backup right now.

157
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:57,060
Finally it's lunchtime.

158
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:00,460
It feels three times longer than usual.

159
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:02,520
I'm starving.

160
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:06,520
Welcome!

161
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:08,400
Here we go.

162
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:09,480
Tendon.

163
00:10:09,480 --> 00:10:11,280
Yes, one tendon coming up.

164
00:10:15,060 --> 00:10:17,760
Free time is about the only
time we get when we're eating.

165
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:19,700
We've been summoned.

166
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,580
Yes, Ryotsu here!

167
00:10:21,580 --> 00:10:25,320
We're starting a meeting,
so get back to the police box right away.

168
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:28,160
But I've only had one
bite of my tendon so far.

169
00:10:28,700 --> 00:10:29,960
Just hurry up and get over here.

170
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:30,720
Yes.

171
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:34,620
Honestly, what a place they've stuck me in.

172
00:10:37,460 --> 00:10:39,080
That'll be 3,150 yen.

173
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:42,980
What? 3,150 yen for one bowl of tendon?

174
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:44,300
Yes.

175
00:10:45,940 --> 00:10:48,420
What an outrageous inflation price!

176
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:52,100
At this rate, I won't last a day
unless I start cooking for myself.

177
00:10:52,820 --> 00:10:56,140
Which one was the police box again?

178
00:10:56,940 --> 00:10:59,920
What? You forgot which police
box you're supposed to return to?

179
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:08,160
Sorry I'm late.

180
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:11,240
You're 28 minutes and 48 seconds late!

181
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:12,100
Yes.

182
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:15,800
People kept stopping me along
the way to ask for directions.

183
00:11:16,420 --> 00:11:18,000
You must have gotten lost.

184
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,260
Just now, they called to ask whether
you're really one of our officers.

185
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:23,920
It's totally obvious, isn't it.

186
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:27,820
So this hub...

187
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:29,760
is a former bureaucrat type,

188
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:34,620
so no matter how much he sneers at me,
Chief Ohara is still better than this.

189
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:41,860
Since then, Ryotsu hasn't
caused any trouble yet, it seems.

190
00:11:41,860 --> 00:11:46,680
Even for Ryo-chan, it hasn't even
been a week since his transfer, has it?

191
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:49,340
You never know with him.

192
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:55,040
Every morning I look at the newspaper and I'm on edge,
wondering if he's caused some trouble.

193
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:57,620
Ryo-san isn't here?

194
00:11:58,140 --> 00:11:59,960
No good, it has to be Ryo-san.

195
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:01,600
But, senior...

196
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:02,780
What is it?

197
00:12:02,780 --> 00:12:04,440
Even if it's not Ryotsu...

198
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:06,440
Feel free to consult us about anything.

199
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:09,300
That's why it has to be Ryo-san.

200
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:11,860
This just stopped working.

201
00:12:11,860 --> 00:12:14,400
I thought Ryo-san would be able to fix it.

202
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:15,940
A remote-control toy

203
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:19,620
This is beyond us.

204
00:12:20,020 --> 00:12:21,180
Is Ryo-san here?

205
00:12:22,740 --> 00:12:24,260
Ryotsu isn't here, I'm afraid.

206
00:12:24,260 --> 00:12:27,180
Please tell us if there's
anything we can do to help.

207
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:29,320
It has to be Ryo-san, no one else will do.

208
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:32,920
Can you even repair a pot with a hole in it?

209
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:34,980
Well, that's a bit much.

210
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:39,020
Without Ryo-chan,
we're hopeless at this sort of thing.

211
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:39,860
Yeah.

212
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:49,280
Wasn't it the police box near Kabuki-za?

213
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:51,640
Still, there are so many people.

214
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:54,660
Is he actually managing to work
properly in a place like this?

215
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,700
So that's the police box.

216
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,280
Alright!

217
00:13:03,060 --> 00:13:03,860
Let's see...

218
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:08,240
This is the First-chome street,
and the road that crosses it is

219
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:09,840
Whew, I'm exhausted.

220
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:12,440
You still can't memorize the map?

221
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:13,360
Idiot!

222
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:17,740
For someone like you, who's studied nonstop since
childhood with cram schools and entrance exams,

223
00:13:17,740 --> 00:13:19,320
memorizing should be your specialty, right?

224
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:22,600
But for someone like me,
who had a wild childhood,

225
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:24,560
this kind of thing is hard.

226
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:27,200
I'm not particularly good at it, though.

227
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:30,700
I'd have thought that much
would sink in naturally.

228
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:33,420
Are you calling me an idiot, you?

229
00:13:34,120 --> 00:13:35,460
N-no, that's not it!

230
00:13:35,460 --> 00:13:36,840
Stop it!

231
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:42,700
But you gave directions at
your last police box too, right?

232
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:44,720
It was downtown before, after all.

233
00:13:44,720 --> 00:13:48,460
Born in the old town, I could memorize
things right away without any maps.

234
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:52,860
Anyway, I've only been to Ginza
about three times in my whole life.

235
00:13:53,220 --> 00:13:54,040
That's extreme.

236
00:13:54,820 --> 00:13:57,260
Why did you leave your last police box?

237
00:13:57,620 --> 00:14:00,760
Well, if I had to name one reason,
it was a personality clash with the Chief.

238
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:02,260
A personality clash

239
00:14:03,540 --> 00:14:06,140
Excuse me, I'd like to ask for directions.

240
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:09,020
Where is Shinbashi Enbujō?

241
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:11,160
Shinbashi Enbujō.

242
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:14,100
Hey, Yamashita, where is it?

243
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:17,120
This is a good chance.
Why don't you look it up yourself?

244
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:20,880
Ugh, damn it, talking like a schoolteacher.

245
00:14:22,020 --> 00:14:23,320
Please wait a moment.

246
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:26,440
I have no idea at all.

247
00:14:27,620 --> 00:14:28,240
Sounds nice, doesn't it.

248
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:32,660
Now I remember!
I think they tore that one down too.

249
00:14:33,020 --> 00:14:34,960
Along with the Nichigeki, quite a while ago.

250
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:36,580
Too bad, old man.

251
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:38,260
Hehehehehehehe.

252
00:14:38,260 --> 00:14:40,900
Ryotsu, stop talking such nonsense.

253
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:43,780
It has to be there,
I'm telling you, absolutely.

254
00:14:43,780 --> 00:14:45,220
A-all right, I get it.

255
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:46,660
Here you go.

256
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:48,440
Thanks.

257
00:14:49,900 --> 00:14:51,760
Just as expected of an attentive officer.

258
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:53,920
Unlike Ryotsu, who

259
00:14:54,820 --> 00:14:55,920
I see.

260
00:14:57,620 --> 00:14:59,640
What do you mean by a personality clash?

261
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:01,080
That.

262
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:04,560
The chief I'm talking
about is that Ohara guy.

263
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:07,740
Anyway, he's spiteful, stubborn,
and a total stick-in-the-mud.

264
00:15:08,340 --> 00:15:11,860
He's angry all year round.
There's no helping the guy.

265
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:13,520
Whenever anything happens,

266
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:15,180
"Hey, Ryotsu!"

267
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:16,860
"Bakaaamaan!"

268
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:20,260
Like a broken record, every single day.

269
00:15:20,260 --> 00:15:23,760
You'd think he'd consider how it
feels for us to have to listen to it.

270
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:26,100
Aren't you the one who's making him angry?

271
00:15:27,620 --> 00:15:29,560
Why is the old man so angry?

272
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:33,100
Well, I'd just like to give
an opinion as a third party,

273
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:37,180
I'm sure the boss is lamenting
that he got such a bad subordinate.

274
00:15:37,660 --> 00:15:39,100
You've got to be kidding.

275
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:42,280
I'm the very picture of diligence, you know.

276
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:45,080
It's the chief who's the hysterical one,
the tyrant,

277
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:47,840
the kind of man whose only pleasure
is scolding his subordinates.

278
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:48,960
What a petty little man.

279
00:15:49,360 --> 00:15:50,540
So it's you?

280
00:15:51,500 --> 00:15:53,660
Just let him talk.

281
00:15:53,660 --> 00:15:54,760
Who's this guy?

282
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:57,600
I'm no longer at the Katsushika police box,
I'm a stranger now.

283
00:15:57,600 --> 00:16:00,580
You said he's neither your boss nor your subordinate,
didn't you?

284
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:01,560
He's the chief, isn't he?

285
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:05,620
As a human being, I'm going to punish you.

286
00:16:05,620 --> 00:16:07,880
That's not fair, dude! It's a cheat!

287
00:16:07,880 --> 00:16:09,060
Shut up, dude!

288
00:16:09,060 --> 00:16:11,380
Hey, wait!

289
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:15,500
Hey, don't make the kid cry!

290
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:18,680
No, he was crying from the start.

291
00:16:19,260 --> 00:16:20,800
What's wrong?

292
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:27,700
He's saying he hates Greta from now on,
or something.

293
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:31,640
I have no idea what's going on.
Anyway, let's take him to the police box.

294
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:35,660
Where'd... d... Kanpuron?

295
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:43,300
Now I'll put that airhead to sleep for good!

296
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:44,800
It's no good.

297
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:48,060
English, Chinese, Mongolian,
none of them get through.

298
00:16:48,060 --> 00:16:48,840
What did you say?

299
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:50,480
What a predicament.

300
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:55,100
Don't cry, don't cry.

301
00:16:55,100 --> 00:16:56,580
Ryotsu, do something!

302
00:16:56,580 --> 00:16:58,480
You're good with kids, right?

303
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:01,200
Yeah, yeah, I know.

304
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:30,200
Heave-ho, yay, yay, yay, yay, yay,
yay, yay, yay, yay, yay, yay, yay...

305
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:34,180
I'll make something even
foreign kids can understand.

306
00:17:34,820 --> 00:17:36,500
Then how about this?

307
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:37,300
It's a horse.

308
00:17:39,340 --> 00:17:41,220
Finally got it

309
00:17:41,220 --> 00:17:42,720
Suho, Suho.

310
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:44,980
So the horse is called Suho?

311
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:46,380
Suho.

312
00:17:46,380 --> 00:17:48,240
Idiot, idiot, idiot!

313
00:17:49,780 --> 00:17:50,660
Suho.

314
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:52,360
I'm Ryotsu.

315
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:53,840
It's Ryotsu.

316
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:55,880
Ryotsu.

317
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:58,040
That's right, Ryotsu.

318
00:17:58,040 --> 00:17:59,280
And you?

319
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:03,840
Ryotsu, Pao.

320
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:08,460
Looks like his name is Pao.

321
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:09,898
Pao Ryotsu,

322
00:18:09,948 --> 00:18:12,760
keep at it and ask where he's from.

323
00:18:12,760 --> 00:18:14,280
Hold on a moment, please.

324
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:19,520
Ryotsu, Japan, Japanese

325
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:20,800
Pao is

326
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:25,080
Pao came to Japan by plane, right?

327
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:26,260
Japan.

328
00:18:26,260 --> 00:18:29,820
Which country did he come from?

329
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:33,140
Mukemuro fuunjarage

330
00:18:33,140 --> 00:18:34,340
Unjarage?

331
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:36,280
Unjarage!

332
00:18:36,380 --> 00:18:39,080
Mue yasu rinpu buwa unjarage!

333
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:44,820
Gurann fubuwa unjarage!

334
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:46,480
I've got it!

335
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:48,580
He came from a country called Unjarage.

336
00:18:48,580 --> 00:18:50,240
Chief, I understand now.

337
00:18:50,240 --> 00:18:51,900
Well done, Ryotsu.

338
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:54,640
I've never heard of a country
called Unjarage, though.

339
00:18:55,180 --> 00:18:58,380
The world is bigger than what's in your head,
you know.

340
00:18:59,180 --> 00:19:02,920
So he came to see kabuki and
got separated from his parents?

341
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:06,200
Kabuki is boring for brats, isn't it?

342
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:08,560
An accident?

343
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:14,920
What the... It's carrying a horse!

344
00:19:14,920 --> 00:19:18,000
I'll handle the accident,
Ryo-san, you take traffic control.

345
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:18,860
Got it.

346
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:23,100
Waaaaah!

347
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:23,300
Waaaaah!

348
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:23,920
Waaaaah!

349
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:25,180
Waaaaah!

350
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:26,980
Waaaaah!

351
00:19:26,980 --> 00:19:28,420
Waaaaah!

352
00:19:28,420 --> 00:19:28,780
Waaaaah!

353
00:19:28,780 --> 00:19:28,980
Waaaaah!

354
00:19:28,980 --> 00:19:29,180
Waaaaah!

355
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:29,840
Catch him!

356
00:19:30,040 --> 00:19:31,300
I know!

357
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:39,640
Don't come over here!

358
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:47,740
This is bad!

359
00:19:47,740 --> 00:19:49,580
Suho! Suho!

360
00:19:50,320 --> 00:19:51,980
Hey! Wait!

361
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:54,280
Suho!

362
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:56,580
Suho noticed! Suho!

363
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:05,960
What the hell!

364
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:10,800
Calm down, you little...!

365
00:20:11,820 --> 00:20:12,500
Stop!

366
00:20:17,180 --> 00:20:17,920
Ryotsu!

367
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:21,800
What was that?

368
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:24,200
Pao?

369
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:25,820
Ryotsu, stop it!

370
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,160
I don't need you to tell me that!

371
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:28,880
Yikes!

372
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:30,240
Yikes!

373
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:33,920
Pao! Watch out!

374
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,720
I'm not just a driver!

375
00:20:35,720 --> 00:20:38,480
Aaaaaaah!

376
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:45,480
Aaaaaaah!

377
00:20:45,480 --> 00:20:46,220
Aaaaaaah!

378
00:20:46,220 --> 00:20:46,740
Aaaaaaah!

379
00:20:46,740 --> 00:20:48,260
Aaaaaaah!

380
00:20:48,260 --> 00:20:50,660
Aaaaaaah!

381
00:20:50,660 --> 00:20:52,980
Eeeeeeeh!

382
00:20:52,980 --> 00:20:55,080
Aaaaaaah!

383
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:00,100
Dessert!

384
00:21:07,980 --> 00:21:10,320
Horse running wild near Ginza 4-chome!

385
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:11,800
Requesting backup, over!

386
00:21:18,820 --> 00:21:19,860
Don't let it get away!

387
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:22,600
Don't let it get away!

388
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:25,500
Aaaaaaah!

389
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:31,080
Where's Ryotsu?

390
00:21:32,440 --> 00:21:33,340
Over there!

391
00:21:45,300 --> 00:21:48,160
Ryotsu

392
00:21:57,980 --> 00:22:01,340
Ryotsu, how do you intend to take
responsibility for this commotion?

393
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:04,040
Responsibility? I'm just

394
00:22:04,040 --> 00:22:05,620
making excuses, that's all.

395
00:22:05,620 --> 00:22:09,200
You've really dragged my name
through the mud this time.

396
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:12,880
I'll have the station chief send
you to the ends of the earth.

397
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:14,440
Now, wait a moment, please.

398
00:22:14,900 --> 00:22:17,000
Ryotsu was only trying to help this child.

399
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:17,880
And you are?

400
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:20,880
I'm Ohara, Ryotsu's former boss.

401
00:22:20,880 --> 00:22:22,320
Chief.

402
00:22:23,940 --> 00:22:25,920
So you're his former superior.

403
00:22:27,500 --> 00:22:30,740
So the failure to properly educate
him is your responsibility, then.

404
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:35,200
Sure, this man is a hopeless idiot,

405
00:22:35,200 --> 00:22:39,180
and he can't speak foreign
languages fluently like you can.

406
00:22:39,660 --> 00:22:43,000
But he and this child understood
each other heart to heart,

407
00:22:43,460 --> 00:22:47,740
and I think that's far more useful
than education that's all talk.

408
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:51,740
Pao

409
00:22:51,740 --> 00:22:53,340
Maron Pao

410
00:22:53,340 --> 00:22:54,960
Pao

411
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:57,180
Thank goodness, thank goodness.

412
00:22:57,500 --> 00:22:58,260
C-Chief!

413
00:22:58,440 --> 00:23:01,080
This boy is Prince Pao of Unjarage!

414
00:23:01,080 --> 00:23:02,720
Prince Pao?!

415
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:06,151
He came incognito with the
king and queen to see kabuki,

416
00:23:06,201 --> 00:23:08,100
and got separated from them.

417
00:23:08,100 --> 00:23:11,101
If anything happens to the prince,

418
00:23:11,151 --> 00:23:13,560
That could have turned
into a serious problem.

419
00:23:14,060 --> 00:23:16,160
So that's how it was, I see.

420
00:23:16,210 --> 00:23:18,360
So it all turned out well, then.

421
00:23:18,360 --> 00:23:19,980
W-well, yeah.

422
00:23:19,980 --> 00:23:20,840
Ryotsu-san.

423
00:23:20,840 --> 00:23:21,620
Yes.

424
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:24,440
After hearing Pao's story,

425
00:23:24,440 --> 00:23:26,820
you are an outstanding police officer.

426
00:23:26,820 --> 00:23:29,520
we sincerely wish for
you to come to our country.

427
00:23:30,820 --> 00:23:32,380
Does that mean... could it be that

428
00:23:35,740 --> 00:23:38,300
I'll go, I'll go,
I'm going to be allowed to go.

429
00:23:38,300 --> 00:23:40,420
Ryotsu, you...

430
00:23:41,020 --> 00:23:42,020
Well then, Chief.

431
00:23:42,020 --> 00:23:43,920
Take care, everyone.

432
00:23:43,920 --> 00:23:45,640
Ryotsu Police Box, effective now.

433
00:23:45,640 --> 00:23:47,020
Wait, that's not "Harem Aee"...

434
00:23:47,020 --> 00:23:49,100
I'm off to the Unjarage Kingdom.

435
00:23:49,980 --> 00:23:51,440
That place is Unjarage!

436
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:54,760
It must be Unjarage!

437
00:23:56,080 --> 00:23:59,060
Everybody, come on over to our country!

438
00:23:59,060 --> 00:24:01,060
Hey, hey,
did they invite you as a police officer?

439
00:24:01,060 --> 00:24:03,340
This isn't what we agreed on!

440
00:24:14,920 --> 00:24:20,220
Like someone calling out,
after the rain stopped,

441
00:24:21,540 --> 00:24:27,060
I walked looking back,
led by the hand of Gaaja,

442
00:24:28,020 --> 00:24:34,280
that strange feeling I had back then.

443
00:24:34,920 --> 00:24:39,500
So on the tiles of the arcade street,

444
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:45,260
I tried walking only on the black ones.

445
00:24:47,720 --> 00:24:51,440
Everyone was a child once,

446
00:24:51,440 --> 00:24:53,580
but everyone has forgotten.

447
00:24:54,480 --> 00:24:57,560
With politicians wearing
their self-important faces,

448
00:24:57,560 --> 00:25:00,860
and even the bulldozer auntie
who's a thorn in my side,

449
00:25:00,860 --> 00:25:03,860
try turning

450
00:25:04,480 --> 00:25:06,440
at that corner.

451
00:25:07,460 --> 00:25:11,660
You can meet everyone, everyone!

452
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:16,280
Over there, it's Kame-ari,

453
00:25:17,340 --> 00:25:19,560
surely Kame-ari!

454
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:24,940
Everyone, come on over to our town!

455
00:25:25,980 --> 00:25:26,380
Thank you!

456
00:25:29,700 --> 00:25:31,900
There you are again, you crackpot professor!

457
00:25:31,900 --> 00:25:32,780
What did you say?

458
00:25:32,820 --> 00:25:35,220
My talent is sleeping inside my head?

459
00:25:35,560 --> 00:25:38,720
So if I put it to work,
I can become a genius?

460
00:25:39,020 --> 00:25:40,200
I see, I see.

461
00:25:40,200 --> 00:25:43,220
So I had hidden power all along.

462
00:25:43,220 --> 00:25:46,560
Next time: Awaken, serious man Ryotsu!

463
00:25:46,560 --> 00:25:47,620
See you then.

464
00:25:51,780 --> 00:25:54,080
Surely Kameari is there!

465
00:25:54,080 --> 00:25:59,280
Come on over, everyone, to our town!

466
00:26:00,120 --> 00:26:00,920
Thank you.

